                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Textbook case of a game with potential but not enough polish to make it enjoyable.\n\nCombat feels like I am just lining up the mouse and sometimes my clicks register as \"damage\". There is little feedback, slow input(melee seems to have a cooldown for some reason. Would rather have long attack animation than quick one with waiting afterwards.) Everything feels sluggish and static.\n\nThe platforming is decent, I haven't had any frusturation with getting where I wanted to go.\n\nAlso doesn't feel that well tested, I often run out of ammo while using only 1-2 shots per enemy, so then I just sit there and spam melee for the rest of the level.\n\nMusic is nice and the graphical style is neat, though I honestly would prefer a non 4:3 screen aspect and a larger resolution but I guess that it's trying to go for a game boy-ey aesthetic.\n\nIf the developer polishes it up and adds more feedback, I would try it again but for now it's just a frusturating game.",
